{"trans": "Promote fair competition, oppose deceit and mutual suspicion, and foster a flourishing diversity of online content; promote unity and collaboration, oppose harming others for personal gain, and promote mutual benefit and win-win outcomes in the online world."}
{"trans": "In conclusion, perhaps more overseas companies believe that going public in the U.S. is not worth the effort, so they choose to withdraw, but this by no means means they are ready to give up the U.S. market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a market environment full of fear and uncertainty, it's extremely difficult for gold to remain untouched, and talking about breaking through the $1,000 level is likely another tale told by a dreamer."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that these students' actions were acts of bravery in the face of danger. They bravely stepped forward to help the elderly man when he was in peril, which was very rare. It is understood that the elderly man has mild mental illness. After the hospital's full efforts to save him, he has now been rescued from critical condition."}
{"trans": "Of course, the above methods are only a few limited and effective approaches in the review process. The arrangements for the review and final push should be diverse and varied, and choices should also be made based on the different characteristics of each candidate. Wishing all candidates success in their exams!"}
{"trans": "It has become another long river of this life and this world, where the Concubine Zhao stepped down from her horse. Sitting on the stones of history, they still speak. The grass is still green as it was, and the flowers still carry their old fragrance. A herd of cattle and sheep do not recognize today, they keep their heads low, modest and cautious. In the meticulous time, we remember the source of our water. People sit in the fragrance of wine, by the autumn waters of Nanhu, where the night is smokeless."}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking a life of comfort or a long lifespan. Since people can only live once, how can one fulfill the meaning and value of life before death? Even if one is shattered to pieces, one should still leave behind a resounding echo, like a jade stone striking the ground with a clear sound, and shine brightly with the light of life in the world."}
{"trans": "Others could remain calm, picking up their spears and scanning the surroundings for enemy movements. Only Li Wenbin was in a panic, stumbling into the grass, his buttocks high in the air, his hands covering his head, looking utterly ridiculous. Those accompanying him couldn't help but cover their faces and laugh. Li Wenbin's authority plummeted instantly."}
{"trans": "\"How do you intend to become a king?\" the animals asked skeptically. \"First, mediate disputes impartially and fairly. Second, handle state affairs diligently and selflessly. Third, when facing strong enemies, lead from the front, charging into battle. This is my campaign speech.\""}
{"trans": "He was experienced in the ways of the world and had endured many hardships, yet he could turn like a compass needle. His North Star was ever-changing and not fixed, and thanks to his charming words that could win people over, he remained vile without ever facing retribution. Moreover, he was eloquent and spoke fluently (unless not paid enough)."}
{"trans": "When I first followed my colleagues to the stock exchange, my fate was sealed, and I became entangled with stocks. Seventeen springs and autumns have made me taste the bitterness, sweetness, sourness, and spiciness of the stock market. After many ups and downs, I have become a veteran. Memories of the past are vivid! 1. There is no end to the sea of suffering; turning back is the shore."}
{"trans": "After a long retreat, the remnants of the army finally stopped. He looked up to the sky and sighed, \"I started my campaign at the age of twenty-five, victorious in every battle, conquering wherever I went. Now, at the twilight of my life, I have suffered such a devastating defeat—it's truly infuriating!\" The news of the victory in the Ningyuan Defense Campaign reached the court, and everyone in the court was overjoyed, raising their cups to celebrate."}
{"trans": "The newlyweds are receiving continuous visits from relatives and friends offering their congratulations. Since the living room's decoration should not be too unconventional, it should primarily focus on comfort and warmth. It should make the couple feel at home and also create a sense of familiarity for their guests. Soft fabric sofas and cushions are essential elements."}
{"trans": "I said, stop overextending the analogy; let's stick to the matter at hand. My son said, over the years, I've been watching your attitude coldly, and I think you regard the computer as something sacred. You're too afraid to touch anything—neither this nor that. For mothers like you, the biggest obstacle to learning is treating the computer as a god."}
{"trans": "Always on edge, fearing to speak wrongly, to act wrongly, or to offend others. The seventh precept of the Eightfold Path is grief; throughout life, various misfortunes often come to mind, leading to sudden sorrow. The eighth precept is suspicion; those with suspicious minds always believe others are scheming against them, being constantly on guard with every word and deed, thus feeling uneasy and often suffering from insomnia."}
{"trans": "The last disgraceful corner still had a pitiful guillotine, shifty and nervous, shamefully furtive, always on edge, as if constantly afraid of being caught in the act—because every time it committed its deeds, it would immediately flee away. How could one not feel relieved at all of this!"}
{"trans": "At this moment, the true charm of a fight lies in the alertness after the challenge, the tense anticipation before the clash, the heated arguments during mediation, the merry toasts after the fight, the magnanimous greetings upon future meetings, and the united front when fighting again. This cycle repeats endlessly, and the ranks of the pacifists grow ever larger."}
{"trans": "The baron's outrageous insults were intolerable; wait, vile wretch, for honor's sake, I shall take upon myself the responsibility of vengeance. Such outrageous insults from all the people can only be avenged by him; even if he loses his life, he cannot endure it silently."}
{"trans": "It seems there will be no argument, no stormy weather; now it's calm. But Mom once again asks inappropriately, \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" Her daughter's reply is also strange and inappropriate: \"Later, good mom, let's see later.\""}
{"trans": "In terms of dealing with the world and people, I am still at an early stage, but when it comes to academic knowledge, he is confident and well-prepared. Even the director, though eloquent, may not be as demanding or peculiar as the professors in a master's thesis defense. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western cuisine, he might be at a loss, but if you ask him how to chop firewood, isn't that something he can easily handle?"}
{"trans": "\"You're about to get your comeuppance for being idle,\" said the ox, and then lowered its head back into the yoke, pulling its cart loaded with fertilizer away. You should live an upright life and always be mindful, never being lazy or idle. If you still don't feel ashamed, you will surely reap the consequences."}
{"trans": "Draw it out, and draw it so vividly and lifelike. His art has repeatedly deceived people's eyes, making them mistake it for real objects at first glance, without realizing it was a painting. For hundreds of years, painting art has always been considered lowbrow and unsuitable for refined taste. It was only through his hands that this art form was once again revived and promoted."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized by people, making them seem sacred and untouchable, mysterious and indescribable. As a result, they are revered as heavenly beings, hence the title \"Son of Heaven.\" In reality, emperors are also human, with both virtues and flaws. Among them, there are enlightened rulers with great talents who stabilize the nation and govern the country, as well as庸碌无能, incompetent tyrants."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he laughed out loud, looking up at the sky and exclaiming, \"Are we really just common mortals?\" The deceit and suspicion in the official world, the hypocrisy of society, and the cold reality all cooled his passionate heart. Could the golden curtain of an \"official scribe\" ever contain his unrestrained and free-spirited soul? Eventually, after enduring the setbacks and pain of his career, he found peace."}
{"trans": "\"A suspicious tramp has been harassing our territory for a long time. He spreads rumors and sows discord. You are to capture this troublemaker and execute him by tomorrow.\" \"We will certainly carry it out, sir.\" The police said and then left. The villain, who was one-eyed, failed to notice that they had been winking at each other while speaking."}
{"trans": "Americans have never treated national leaders as gods, nor have they obeyed them blindly. However, Obama yielded to the expectations of his supporters. He also believed that he was the long-awaited savior they had been waiting for. The silence of the people hit him hard. But the intoxicating feeling of rising to power almost made him lose his sense of self."}
{"trans": "The normally smiling Taurus man is practical to the core and can't stand betrayal of being disloyal. Don't try to probe his true feelings. The steady ox is content to graze and eat grass, smiling at you just as Jesus looks at his sheep. If you don't want the scene to turn into a bullfight in Spain, with blood flowing and the field littered with corpses, don't ever make him jealous."}
{"trans": "Gemini wouldn't have any fun in life if he didn't play some little tricks or use a bit of cunning. Though he appears carefree and casual on the surface, once things get complicated, he will strike you unexpectedly. While everyone fights fiercely and gets hurt, he remains calm and benefits from the situation. But once he achieves success and draws everyone's attention, he'll suddenly act like a carefree prince, leaving you behind and playing the game of luring and then letting go."}
{"trans": "In reality, given that Germany is part of the eurozone and bound by the euro, the idea of Germany looking out for its own interests alone is sheer fantasy. Initially, the creation of the eurozone was based on the grand vision of shared prosperity. Now, the Greek debt crisis has triggered the European debt crisis, and the idea that one country's loss becomes another's is only natural. When the gate of a city burns, the fish in the pond suffer as well; and with fires raging all around, some areas are almost reduced to ashes."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in major commodities may be the most direct and effective way to hedge against inflation. However, when it comes to investing in commodities, the stories that often come to mind are usually alarming. There are cases of people losing everything in commodity futures trading, and airlines suffering massive losses from hedging crude oil. Such incidents are numerous, making commodity investment seem highly risky and unattainable for ordinary people."}
{"trans": "The vast sky tolerates the rampant thunder and lightning, thus giving rise to calm winds and bright sunshine; the boundless sea endures the fierce waves, thus creating gentle ripples; the silent forest accepts the cruelty of the strong preying on the weak, thus bringing forth the fragrance of flowers and the songs of birds. The sky, the sea, and the forest achieve their beauty and extraordinariness precisely because they understand tolerance, know when to step back, and humble themselves to accept. When you humble yourself, the world becomes wide and expansive."}
{"trans": "Looking at the changing trends and dynamics of the college entrance examination in recent years, what we need is to firmly grasp the new tendencies and directions in the exam questions, plan ahead, move from seeing things through a foggy haze to seeing them clearly. Only then can you be confident with a million soldiers at your command, fight bravely on the battlefield, and defeat the enemy with a smile. With the guidance of renowned teachers, transform ordinary into extraordinary. A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; a nine-story pagoda starts with a pile of earth. Let us help you take the first step toward successful review for the college entrance examination!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself is equivalent to possessing the golden key to happiness. Appreciating yourself is not being self-centered, nor is it being arrogant, nor is it being intoxicated by oneself; appreciating yourself even less means being stuck in old ways. Give yourself some confidence, some joy, and a smile. Why worry about lacking happiness in life? Frequently celebrate yourself and learn to find pleasant moods."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people have gradually realized that the internet and traditional industries are not bitter rivals but can complement each other perfectly, like the \"two outstanding beauties\" in harmony. The retail industry is gradually showing characteristics of channel integration, with increasing mutual penetration and integration between online and offline channels. Currently, Taobao has opened offline stores, and traditional enterprises entering the internet are numerous, like fish crossing a river. From Gome and Suning Appliances to Walmart and Carrefour supermarkets, there are many examples."}
{"trans": "In conclusion, uncertainties in the commodity market are constantly emerging, and financial hegemony still manipulates the market, with game rules changing frequently. Against the backdrop of global debt crisis and mixed prospects for global economic recovery, the US dollar remains the main factor influencing the trend of commodity prices. The economic policies of the US and Europe are closely linked, while domestic regulatory measures further amplify the situation. The interplay of these three factors is bound to lead to significant volatility in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "Chinese red is a profound spiritual culture, unique to the Chinese people. It represents a powerful force—self-reliance, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and perseverance. It embodies the enduring quality of the Chinese nation, characterized by noble integrity that has been passed down for thousands of years. As a leading furniture enterprise, Liantianhong passionately spreads the fire of Chinese red. With the business philosophy of integrity as the foundation, it was the first to implement transparent workshop production, setting an industry benchmark and revitalizing the appearance of the furniture industry."}
{"trans": "Physical characteristics: In \"Journey to the West,\" Tang Sanzang is tall and dignified, with refined manners and a kind nature, possessing profound knowledge of Buddhism. During his western journey to obtain scriptures, he faced eighty-one trials, yet remained steadfast in his devotion. With the assistance of his disciples, Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing, he endured countless hardships and finally succeeded in retrieving the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, also known as the Monkey Pilgrim, is Tang Sanzang's senior disciple. He has fiery eyes and golden pupils, can transform into seventy-two different forms, and can ride clouds. He is fierce in punishing evil, fearless of difficulties, tenacious, and brave."}
{"trans": "III. Attitude towards studying: I have my own set of experiences - \"cultivating a sense of problems\" and \"avoiding staying up late.\" In fact, once learning becomes proficient, although it may not be effortless, it can at least give us a sense of confidence. I do not advocate for the method of doing a large number of problems, because there is no need to repeatedly solve similar questions. We only need to compare and think deeply about similar problems, and summarize the methods to solve such questions. What is called \"sense of problems\" is similar to the \"language sense\" we often mention in English."}
{"trans": "The world's longest man-made structure—the Great Wall of China. The majestic Great Wall of China stretches across the mountainous ridges of northern China, with a total length of more than 6,700 kilometers. It was initially constructed during the Spring and Autumn Period and Warring States Period. It is a rare ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture, renowned for its long history, grand scale, and magnificent grandeur. It was listed by UNESCO as a \"World Heritage Site\" and is hailed as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "Because of capital, they remain low-key; because of their uniqueness and inability to conform to the commonplace, they remain low-key. Essentially, luxury goods are exceptional, even unparalleled, allowing for no compromise in quality or in the embodiment of fashion. They also possess impeccable superiority in artistic and stylistic culture. Luxury goods can certainly not be considered essential items in life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and deep brand heritage absolutely make them indispensable in life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as if they were weighed down by lead, she still strode confidently through the street toward the parking garage. Now, drowsy and alone, she drove along the fluorescent-lit concrete driveway, feeling her mind growing hazy. Seventeen hours ago, when she had parked here, there were two station wagons parked on either side, so close together that she had had to wriggle awkwardly out of her car. Now her old \"Taurus\" sat alone like an orphan in the eighth-level parking area."}
{"trans": "A decade ago, perhaps no one could imagine that the Internet could move with laptop computers, just as people couldn't imagine phones fitting into pockets and accompanying modern life at all times twenty years ago. Today, various smart terminals are radiating unprecedented magic, subtly changing human lifestyles. In the next decade, disruptive innovations are likely to emerge in fields such as terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics!"}
{"trans": "We advocate team spirit and also admire the heroic spirit of risking everything to save teammates. However, we must ensure that we do not become a burden or a liability to our teammates. We should try our best to avoid putting our teammates in unnecessary danger while trying to rescue us. Strict training and the ability to make immediate decisions in the field are absolutely essential! Before you've experienced the real thing—gunfire and bullets—don't play around with your theoretical talk in front of us. Some things are not something you, a newly graduated student officer, can understand!"}
{"trans": "I regret not fully understanding the five-character poems about the poplar tree and my grandfather's seven-character poems. Although I have been accumulating knowledge and making progress in the art of \"pretending to be ignorant,\" I have not yet achieved complete enlightenment. Last night, my neck was bitten by a mute mosquito, and I shouted loudly: \"How can you bite me silently? How can you suck blood without being open and honest? How can you learn to be a proper mosquito and rush toward my neck proudly and boldly?\" Therefore, I live a life that is both tiring and absurd, often hearing the mocking laughter of mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "As barbecue stalls spring up like mushrooms in every corner of the city, people's nights have become increasingly flavorful. However, it's really difficult to enjoy both delicious food and a refined atmosphere. As the sun sets and the sky turns red, blending with the lush green grass of the soccer field, under such a beautiful scene, tables are neatly arranged according to the terrain. The barbecue chefs skillfully grill the meat, waiters move around briskly, and customers chat and laugh happily, fully immersed in comfort. Soft music plays in the background, adding a romantic and charming mood."}
{"trans": "Hearing me say all that, the old gentleman let out a long sigh: \"Hei, I've lived through nine deaths and one life, it's really hard to put into words!\" Thus, this old gentleman, who was proud and stubborn, finally opened up his bumpy life and inner world to me, a writer he had never met before... In his sometimes passionate, sometimes heavy, sometimes tearful, and sometimes laughing narration, I felt the life of a seventy-year-old man who had experienced much hardship, his grand and tragic life, and the inevitable fate that he couldn't resist..."}
{"trans": "It appears that the political arena in the West is far from as clean as people imagine. Beneath the appearance of integrity flows a torrent of corruption, albeit with a uniquely Western flavor. Politicians solemnly \"sow\" their seeds on stage, while harvesting their rewards reasonably and legally off stage. The seasoned politicians and shrewd capitalists work in perfect harmony, understanding each other without needing to speak. The game of reciprocity between officials and businessmen, and the art of money and power transactions, has reached an extremely sophisticated level. It is so sophisticated that it has become open and legal, so sophisticated that even Western democracy and the rule of law are powerless to deal with it."}
{"trans": "After wading through the water for several hours, a vast, open cavern suddenly came into view. \"My God, this isn't just an underground cave—it's like an underground forest!\" the team members shouted in awe. The cavern was as large as a basketball court, with uneven ground covered in scattered rocks, flowing water, and deep ravines. Towering stone pillars, some as thick as a bowl, reached over ten meters high. Massive stone curtains, jagged stone hanging formations, and twisted stone columns filled the space, each more bizarre than the last, resembling a primeval forest. In addition, numerous crystal formations sparkled under the lights, creating an enchanting atmosphere that made it feel like entering a fairy tale world."}
{"trans": "The size of the heart can be vast, capable of holding a whole world, or it can be shrunk to the smallest size, only able to contain a home, a person, a sesame seed, a drop of virus. A single raindrop can drown it. A single gust of wind can shatter it. A single rumor can make it suffer unbearably. A single conspiracy can reduce it to eternal ruin. The heart can be very hard, harder than any known metal in the world. It can be very soft, like a weeping silk or a delicate piece of brocade. It can be very resilient, enduring hundreds of times of damage and委屈, still remaining flat and untouched. It can be very fragile, and with just a little carelessness, it can crumble into dust."}
{"trans": "Strolling through, one is greeted by dense shade, vibrant flowers vying for beauty, and a serene, tranquil scenery that is breathtakingly beautiful. The gentle breeze carries a fragrant aroma, instantly bringing a sense of peace and relaxation. The winding stone paths lead to secluded spots, with flowers and trees arranged in harmonious disorder. The clear and melodious sound of flowing water adds to the charm, as multiple scenic elements intertwine in three dimensions, forming a vivid and fragrant picture of life. As one moves, the scenery changes continuously; every flower, leaf, grass, tree, stone, and spring exudes a unique charm, allowing one to escape the hustle and bustle of the world and experience the beauty of unity between heaven and humanity, cleansing the soul. Wandering among these beautiful sights, one fully enjoys the joys of life."}
{"trans": "The previously enraged whaling ship said, \"This is the whale we caught.\" The currently smug whaling ship said, \"Then why is it here?\" The previously enraged one said, \"It escaped again.\" The currently smug one said, \"Who didn't tie it properly.\" The previously enraged one said:"}
{"trans": "Your conceited and greedy nature cannot be concealed by your dignified appearance! The pretending doctors, the babbling witches, and the eloquent frauds are all mocking our incompetence—watch out for the slap! You, ungrateful husbands, think yourselves clever. You despise love and goodness;"}
{"trans": "A two-month farce has come to an end, but we are not clear why Foxconn is so angry about these two reports. Well-funded companies are not short of advisory teams, and crisis management tactics can be as dramatic as expressing anger rather than just emotional appeals. Perhaps it's to serve as a warning to others, or perhaps it's a distraction tactic."}
{"trans": "Rewarding merit with titles and granting honors. Fine food and delicious delicacies should belong to it. \"I pity you and find you ridiculous,\" the duck said, \"you are overly arrogant. Your view is biased. We wild ducks fly across the world, free from attachments, living anywhere. You, however, depend on others. We support ourselves, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the most difficult. It should be abrupt and vigorous, straightforward and to the point, sharp and incisive, to captivate the reader. There is no need to go around in circles or to use empty phrases. He also told me that when explaining a difficult issue, if one uses a metaphor, all the tangled arguments will be resolved at once. How economical and skillful that is! Such thoughts are typical of him."}
{"trans": "She took up the divination seriously. After a moment of bustling activity, she pretended to examine the sand tray again, calculated once more, and then looked up at Kudi, saying, \"You damned, shameless scoundrel! Dare you speak so recklessly before me? The divination clearly states that you are called Kudi, a bandit who commits murder and robbery, does no good, and is utterly wicked.\""}
{"trans": "The castle indeed resembled a paradise away from the world. He gazed at the magnificent architecture and felt a mixture of admiration and awe. They wandered through the garden, picking fresh fruits and enjoying the atmosphere filled with birdsong and floral fragrance, so engrossed that they lost track of time. When they finally leisurely explored the entire castle, it was already dark, and they returned to the hall by the pond, intending to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning works quite well. The cool, fresh air, the well-organized layout, the neatly dressed guests, and the polite waiters all make this place feel like a hidden paradise, exceptionally comfortable. The only thing spoiling the atmosphere is people. Those neatly dressed gentlemen are all fat and gluttonous, which is quite unpleasant to watch. They all nod to Nikolai, and for some reason, some of them even give him a glance."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver, watching their resources dwindle and realizing their fate was sealed, finally abandoning resistance and fleeing toward the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth, sweeping away the remaining enemies. They were like two proud and unstoppable land dragons, crushing everything in their path, reducing enemy strongholds to flat ground and sending the slow ones to their deaths. They were a stirring declaration of victory for the Chinese army, announcing the approaching end of the stubborn aggressors."}
{"trans": "After this ordeal, our family never recovered; our fortune declined, we fell into poverty and hardship, struggling through hunger and cold. The old locust tree lost its former luster, and the remaining half of its stump stood alone, isolated, and forlorn in the partially desolate courtyard. It was left to endure wind and rain, cold dew and frost, listless for many years, neither sprouting new buds nor growing branches, and no one paid it any attention. It could only stand straight and stiff, \"looking up to the sky and sighing longingly.\""}
{"trans": "Everything reactionary will not fall unless you strike it. Dust won't disappear on its own unless you sweep it away. You're all doomed, but me, Zhang Puqing, the loyal Bolshevik, upright in character, clean-handed, with three hearts and two intentions, four legs on the ground, five bodies on the ground, six sixes, seven seven events, eight immortals crossing the sea, nine provinces and states, ten perfects. Ha ha, revolution is not a banquet, not writing an article, not painting or embroidery, not frying oil noodles. The proletariat has completely taken power over all of you, these devils and demons."}
{"trans": "Over-praising college entrance examination top scorers may make them feel superior to others. Some may develop a sense of self-satisfaction, become arrogant and self-centered, and unconsciously relax their self-discipline in future work and life, thus becoming stagnant and difficult to cooperate with others. Others may believe that they can never be worse than others at any time, and pursue perfection excessively, being overly cautious and hesitant in their actions, strictly following rules and regulations. All of these may lead former top scorers to lack creativity and enthusiasm in their work, ultimately making them difficult to achieve great success."}
{"trans": "I will treat every patient of mine equally, regardless of whether his clothes are luxurious or tattered, whether his appearance is handsome or ugly, whether he is wealthy or impoverished, whether his status is high or low, whether he is spotless or battered, whether he suffers from a complicated illness or a minor ailment, whether he is polite or rude to me, whether he is well-mannered or illiterate, whether he is humorous or reserved, whether he is a high-ranking official or just an ordinary citizen..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that uncontrollable longing, that deep affection through thick and thin, that sincere devotion in times of hardship — these are the deepest comfort and the strongest support in life. And all of these are free. They are something money cannot buy. A goal is also free. Whether you are a prince with fine clothes and delicacies or a homeless child with nothing to cover your body, as long as you are willing, you can set a goal for your life. This goal can be great or ordinary, glorious or simple — as long as you are willing, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should focus your mind, plan the path to success, and then move forward with full commitment. During this process, you must not be fickle-minded, indecisive, or easily swayed by distractions. You should strictly eliminate doubt and fear, as they will undermine your determination, disrupt your emotional state, and hinder your efforts to achieve your goals. People filled with doubt and fear will ultimately achieve nothing and end up with nothing. When feelings of doubt and fear infiltrate your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all your strong thoughts will be severely impacted and eventually collapse."}
{"trans": "A cultivated person holds deep respect, reverence, and admiration for the many admirable qualities of humanity, such as loyalty, courage, trust, diligence, mutual assistance, self-sacrifice, fearlessness in danger, endurance of hardship, and steadfast determination. Not everyone can embody these virtues in practice, but they understand and cherish them, and they can sing praises of them. Humans are not necessarily incapable of cowardice and laziness, but they must not disguise these vices as noble virtues. One cannot denounce all those who have achieved these virtues as hypocrites simply because one himself fails to reach them. You may kneel in the mud, but you must not smear the mud onto the entire world's chest and then solemnly declare that everything is dirty."}
{"trans": "This world has beginnings that are quiet and subtle, ones that are grand and dramatic, ones that are cautious and careful, ones that are bold and decisive, ones that are secretive and concealed, ones that are hesitant and reluctant, ones that are full of ulterior motives, and ones that are open and straightforward. Every segment of life's journey and every event in life is given a unique starting style by different people. These styles reflect one's temperament, perspective, courage, demeanor, and breadth of mind in managing life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the final stage of review plays a crucial role in the entire preparation process. Therefore, we should place great importance on the last stage of review and avoid making mistakes that could lead to the failure of all previous efforts and miss the opportunity for success. The following explains several common misconceptions."}
{"trans": "The market is currently leaderless, with major sectors taking turns in adjustment, weak support, and great difficulty for mainstream capital in operations, making the overall market very weak. It is like a startled bird, and once there are some negative news, it panics and sells in fear, leading to increased panic selling. Meanwhile, funds outside the market continue to watch and wait. Plus, before the holiday, the desire to buy is not strong, so market sentiment is even more scattered."}
{"trans": "The stubborn Japanese, already on their last legs, were barely holding on, their tenuous front line resembling a battle-scarred warship leaking water from all sides. This fatal blow immediately shattered them like weathered rock. In fact, preventing the armored train from advancing was not difficult; it was simply a matter of dismantling the tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Fish Eyes Among Real Ones: How to Identify Authentic from Fake? The popularity of cultural relics and nuts has been increasing, with the market price rising continuously. Many fake products are made using high-tech methods. Old Hu used to be deceived at first, but now he has become well-informed and experienced. He even sleeps with nuts in his hands every night, and almost nothing can deceive him anymore. He has shared several methods for identifying genuine from fake with the readers of the evening newspaper."}
{"trans": "In my lifetime, I have walked through the same paths as others: the broad sunny road and the narrow wooden bridge. I have gone through ups and downs, twists and turns, and come through them all. I cannot help but admit that I have had good luck; the success I have achieved and the empty fame I have gained are somewhat not up to the name. On the other hand, my misfortunes have also been far beyond what ordinary people can endure. During that notorious so-called \"great revolution,\" because I dared to speak up for justice, I almost lost my life. The physical pain I endured is something I will never forget."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can be considered one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. When he compared himself to Guan Zhong in Longzhong, how confident he was! His prediction of the division of the Three Kingdoms was remarkably accurate. When he first stepped out of his cottage, he faced Xiah Hou Dun's army of over 100,000 troops without fear. He set fire to Bolong Slope, winning the admiration of Guan Yu and Zhang Fei. He burned Xinye, causing Cao Ren to be terrified. With the clever strategy in the silk pouch, he outwitted Zhou Yu three times, showing both wisdom and humor. He remained loyal, even though he was granted special permission by Liu Bei, he never declared himself emperor. Due to a decision-making error, he was forced to implement the Empty City Stratagem, and his calmness was truly admirable. However, what moves me the most is not these, but the \"Autumn Wind at Wu Zhang Plains.\""}
{"trans": "As soon as night falls in the mountain village, we can hear sharp, continuous barking from the dogs. After the midnight hour, the barking becomes faint and intermittent, and the lights in the windows flicker on one after another, as if they were white, clean faces like the heart of a cabbage... The moonlight is also washing its face by the water pipe in the courtyard..."}
{"trans": "Close-range shots miss; header chances in front of goal mysteriously go wide; even one-on-one opportunities are missed... Lacking sufficient experience in domestic league competitions, the young national team's ability to seize chances in attack leaves much to be desired, which is currently the biggest weakness of this squad."}
{"trans": "But in a sociological sense, the current Israeli and Palestinian sides are enemies who hate each other. This is due to the estrangement, coldness, suspicion, and hostility caused by the dispersion of Jews from Palestine in 556 BCE, which separated the two brothers and prevented them from seeing each other for over a thousand years. It is also due to the return of Jews to Palestine two thousand years later to establish the state of Israel. As a result, the struggle between them turned into mutual slaughter, and the brotherly affection was completely erased."}
{"trans": "National policies descend from above, and the industry situation takes a sharp turn for the worse. Ceramic production areas are hit first, like fierce beasts trapped in a困境, struggling in the产区 and ceramic enterprises seeking their way out. The cold wave brings impact and pain to the产区, but also makes them more clearly see the path ahead. Read more: The industry situation takes a sharp turn for the worse, with ceramic production areas struggling like trapped beasts."}
{"trans": "Stepping into the Suzhou garden, one wanders through the courtyards of Suzhou, encountering scenes such as small bridges over flowing water, white-walled and dark-tiled houses, winding paths leading to secluded spots, and twisting paths with ever-changing views. The most profound impression is that its meticulous and refined garden-making process is remarkably similar to that of the imperial gardens in the Forbidden City. The arrangement of corridors, pavilions, and pavilions is layered and well-ordered; walking along a 20-meter path gives the feeling of a vast open space of three or five miles, creating an illusion of wandering through a painting."}
{"trans": "The battlefield situation is ever-changing, and there are no fixed rules for winning battles throughout history. How to deploy troops, command forces, choose between attack and defense, between positional warfare and mobile warfare, whether to proactively abandon a position or hold it firmly, which local areas to give up and which to defend—these decisions should all be left to the front-line commanders to make, and the supreme commander should not interfere excessively. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be integrated and flexibly applied. It's hard to say which method is definitely superior. This is what is meant by \"there are many paths to Rome\"—the only hard truth is that winning the battle is the ultimate criterion."}
{"trans": "Novels are the backlight of the soul. You inject part of your soul into your work, giving it your flesh and blood, and thus achieving a high level of art. This involves two issues. First, writers need to examine their true state of soul and should first shape themselves. Second, the power of sincerity is immense. Sincerity here not only means correcting excesses but also means rejecting artificiality, flattery, pandering, and opportunism in the literary atmosphere. Don't scratch an itch with a boot on the shoe, don't talk nonsense, and don't sell sincerity as dog skin ointment. I think sincerity should be a way of living, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The old槐 tree by the window, weathered by wind and storms, stands motionless as the moon, also motionless, hangs on the槐 branches like a bell yet so far from the sound of a bell. I know that all fragments should not be expected to make a resounding impact when cast upon the ground. Yet it is precisely these fragment-like moonbeams that make the silent midnight more like a midnight shipwreck."}
{"trans": "Cruel, merciless, deceitful, and sinister, yet I am compassionate, benevolent, and devoted to saving all beings. In the eerie castle of Dus, my soul inscribes spells and characters with intense focus, when suddenly I hear the painful cry of Dulcinea from Toboso, and I learn that she has unfortunately been cursed by magic."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dandan suspects that Alibaba has the嫌疑 of \"crossing the river and breaking the bridge.\" \"Capital has its nature, and it is natural for them to consider the interests of their shareholders. Taking over an investment means taking on the capital contract. You cannot worship them as gods when you need them, but condemn them as demons when they hinder you.\""}
{"trans": "A keen eye cannot help but be overwhelmed! The gaze is confused, and one dares not look directly at the throne. We come from the East, yet the incident occurs in the West; the ranks are vast and long—看不到头尾. One falls, another rises; they rush forward in competition, brimming with courage, wielding lances, fighting ten to one, a hundred to ten, countless lives vanish without a trace."}
{"trans": "He had just managed to seize the ancestral jade green stone and was reveling in his triumph when he had to go on a long trip due to some matter. When he returned home, he only learned from his family that the ancestral jade green stone along with a bag of gold and silver had vanished without a trace. Upon hearing this news, he flew into a rage, scolded and beat himself up, and even tore his clothes. The more he thought about having wasted his efforts like trying to scoop water with a bamboo basket, the angrier he became."}
{"trans": "2008, an extraordinary year. On the battlefield of public relations and marketing for domestic enterprises, it was also a year filled with fierce struggles. For corporate market public relations personnel, it seemed as if \"public relations crises\" suddenly arrived like a fierce flood, causing fear and anxiety. Time flies forward rapidly, and soon we are about to step into 2009. Looking back on this year, perhaps many business owners still feel lingering fear, walking on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leo friends are almost always willing to help at work, ready to lend a hand as long as they can showcase their talents. However, this tendency can easily lead to forgetting things and accumulating a huge workload. Therefore, having a handy planner and weekly schedule is the most appropriate and auspicious tool for them. Especially those with a lively and childlike style perfectly match their pure and innocent nature. Even when busy, they can handle everything effortlessly and with ease."}
{"trans": "A good composition should include six or seven excellent sentences: first, vivid and beautiful similes; second, grand and majestic parallel sentences; third, emotionally rich personification sentences; fourth, sentences with profound cultural references; fifth, enlightening philosophical sentences; sixth, contrasting sentences that complement each other; and seventh, poetic and elegant sentences. Skillfully using these excellent sentences can make the writing concise yet meaningful, striking the key points, illuminating the entire piece, and achieving tenfold effect with one sentence, naturally enhancing the literary quality."}
{"trans": "Even more absurd is the fact that today, Western countries' economies are still in a deadlock, with their printing presses ready to churn out more money, their finances already running out of rice, yet they still rely on China to \"feed the world.\" Everyone now turns their gaze toward China, the world's second-largest economy. If the global system dominated by the United States after the Cold War has fallen into a desperate state, will this emerging superpower step up to the challenge? Or will it let the West suffer the consequences on its own? But this time, China might be unable to do much despite its intentions."}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, ruled for fifty-four years, expanding the territory and forming a vast empire stretching from the central part of the Korean Peninsula in the east to the shores of Lake Balkhash today in the west, from the heartland of Vietnam in the south to the area along the line of Saiyin Shanda in Outer Mongolia in the north. The population under his rule reached nearly sixty million. To be fair, among hundreds of Chinese emperors, those who could expand the territory as Emperor Wu of Han did are truly rare. Others could be considered fortunate if they merely managed to preserve the empire without committing acts of national humiliation and disgrace. In this sense alone, Emperor Wu of Han can be regarded as a great and capable emperor."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the mundane aspects of everyday life, lacking dramatic twists and turns, yet they offer a fresh, unique perspective and an unmistakable personal bias, giving them a sense of novelty. He is skilled at creating individualized, distinctive characters, which is precisely the hallmark of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people make a big show of themselves, using exaggerated claims and grandiose rhetoric, constantly seeking to highlight their uniqueness, packaging themselves and endlessly promoting and selling themselves amidst the flood of information. Others, however, adopt a mindset of keeping their wealth hidden, focusing on self-cultivation, concealing their talents, accumulating strength and waiting for the right moment, quietly working hard without making a sound."}
{"trans": "In fact, why do \"verbal battles\" always erupt widely and persist for months without ceasing? What forces are behind pushing them forward? What exactly is subtly influencing the judgments and thoughts of netizens? Not only ordinary netizens, but even some website managers are puzzled by this."}
{"trans": "That night, he spread out his writing paper, ready to write an article to reclaim those 20 yuan. The title of his article that night was \"On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality.\" He said: \"In this age of decadent material desires, we must raise the banner of morality to oppose the enslavement by material things.\" That night, his essay surged forward with intense passion and sorrow, subtly guiding, fervently expressing, painfully heartfelt, sincere and open, fierce and unrestrained, smooth and flowing, like a torrent rushing forward..."}
{"trans": "1. The analytical essay should have a forward-looking perspective. As an official-style article, the most fundamental characteristic of the analytical essay is to have a high-minded stance and a lofty theme. When writing the analytical essay, one should focus on long-term interests, look beyond surface phenomena to grasp the essence, be adept at viewing matters from a lofty perspective, and be skilled at elevating the theme. In other words, the article should reflect a noble ideological realm and must never be媚俗 (conformist to vulgar trends), let alone be lowbrow and vulgar, spreading complaints and grievances."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a compassion shown to the sufferers. When he smiles, his smile resembles the yearning of those seeking the unknown, like the dust of stars falling into the eyes of children, or like a piece of bread in the throat."}
{"trans": "Look up again, how graceful her shoulders are! They resemble twin lambs or two jade peaks; as slender as autumn mountains and as smooth as autumn waters. Above the shoulders, we reach the face, the part that is generally praised and sung about."}
{"trans": "Even lotus flowers have suffered the tragedy of exterminating nine clans. Lotus after lotus, the thousand fingers of the lotus petals clung to a summer, then released another summer. Now it is the ghostly rain of autumn night, pattering down onto the broken pond scum, like a disheveled, blind-eyed Chopin abusing the thousand keys of the piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moonlight, the essence becomes more profound; discussing swords under the moonlight, one's heart and courage become more sincere; discussing poetry under the moonlight, the charm becomes more subtle; facing a beauty under the moonlight, one's affection becomes more sincere. The way to appreciate the moon: when it is bright and clear, it is suitable to look up; when it is hazy and dim, it is suitable to look down. Spring wind is like wine; summer wind is like tea; autumn wind is like smoke; winter wind is like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rode the tide of blood, arriving in this damp and cold world on a single red boat, gracefully descending. His final leap was shot out of the gate of life by a surging wave of heat, like the mud and sand rushing down during a flood. The infant's excited cry sounded like glass cups colliding and shattering."}
{"trans": "If China has one more melancholic writer, this north-facing study should be held responsible. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a refrigerator full of southern fruits, preserved and pregnant. By day, I seem to be immersed in the ocean floor, where the silent darkness plays a gray melody."}
{"trans": "The red candle has a soul; it does not spare its life, yet it is especially attached to life. Whenever it is about to burn out, the charred wick would strangely arch high in the flame, convulsively and proudly, as if a warrior suddenly struck down had frozen in mid-air into an unyielding sculpture, then sank heavily into a pool of fiery blood..."}
{"trans": "Looking out into the sky, it has its own经纬 (meridians and parallels) and self-regulates its behavior. After the morning dew and rain, the sun emerges, with silver beads densely attached, all shining brightly, one sun giving birth to countless suns. The old web in the corner need not be swept; let the dust settle. Over time, the ropes thicken, resembling the roots of an old tree, forming a three-dimensional mural. Read the traditional, read the modern, always fresh and new."}
{"trans": "Spring is always the first to knock on the bamboo gate of the garden, then lights one by one the torches that were extinguished last year. At this time, the lonely winter, like a凄厉的 wolf, retreats in the sudden flames. The flames leave its lonely gaze directionless, and the earth's floral skirt leads it astray."}
{"trans": "The means of punishing evil are more evil than evil itself; killing the innocent is as easy as cutting grass. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, chastity, and righteousness, there is a sea of blood and swords. The grandeur and magnificence come at the cost of corpses scattered everywhere. The basic value of life is just a few withered grasses under a horse's hoof; the survival rights of the common people are merely a few bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "—The heavenly melody, infinite mystery, the infinite enclosing the finite, or God's severe yet tender command. Music is the omnipotent and omniscient God of notes, both Creator—who arranges and defines the position of each note—and Saviour—who, if the notes could listen and follow the ceaseless melody, would be saved."}
{"trans": "Above the winding lotus pond, there stretches an expanse of dense leaves. The leaves rise high out of the water, like the skirts of gracefully dancing girls. Among the layers of leaves, there are scattered white flowers; some are gracefully blooming, others modestly closed like buds. They resemble pearls, stars in the blue sky, or beauties just emerging from a bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, for a city, if everything you encounter and see is young and bright, it must be that the time is not yet right, and the strings are not in harmony. This is similar to writing; when adjectives are like a young lady in full makeup and parallel structures are like lovers standing side by side, it certainly means one has not yet entered the realm of writing. The pinnacle of writing is like an old street with sparse ginkgo trees, an old seat beneath the tree, and idle conversation among the seats, refined yet relaxed."}
{"trans": "The suffering of individual families does not affect the world's happiness. Summer rushes in uncontrollably, and the flowers of the hibiscus bloom like pink confetti, brushing against the lonely and desolate window sill of the病房. The girl's head has become a polygon, with already healed bone seams resembling cracked earth, stretching out black holes beneath thin skin. An inner demon expands in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a refrigerator full of tropical fruits. During the day, I seem to be immersed in the ocean floor, where the silent darkness plays a gray melody. At night, I seem to hear the sound of Inuit sleds gliding across the snow, and the long beard of the North Star swings down, ringing a series of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the bright moon, not wanting to disturb anyone, yet they genuinely disturb a wide area around them. This can truly be called \"the moon rising startles mountain birds.\" Compared to Tao Yuanming's quietness, Wang Wei's quietness carries a bit more nobility and a bit more refined design. His brilliance lies in being nobler than the common people and more natural than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even the brown coffee table was painted with emotion, a gentle, long rectangular shape, bearing all the lively activities on top. There was another larger one, also with white magnolia blossoms, thin and bright, looking like a jade fish that Grandmother Yang kept in her mouth when she had a toothache, cool and refreshing. The forsythia displayed strong, vigorous lines, opening and closing with determination. It exercises control over life with calmness and dominance."}
{"trans": "\"Vast and boundless, returning to the great wilderness!\" When I read this passage, I didn't feel sad, but rather a sense of beauty, a kind of beauty similar to reading about Jing Ke in \"Records of the Grand Historian\" who wore white clothes and crossed the Yi River to assassinate King Qin. It was filled with vivid colors. Imagine a young man from a wealthy family who has seen through the world's illusions, standing barefoot in the snow, wearing a red cloak, bowing farewell to his father—how beautiful that would be!"}
{"trans": "We cannot pass by that dark, humiliating, and indifferent era of Chengde, just as when approaching the Mogao Caves, we are inevitably faced with that ugly and desolate Daoist Tower. No matter how brilliant and magnificent the memories of Dunhuang may be, they can never fill the vast emptiness of the Caves of the Hidden Scriptures, nor can they wash away the pale sorrow in the Thousand Buddha Caves, nor can they heal the ancient wounds of the people on the horizon, where blood has long been shed."}
{"trans": "Forgetfulness visits us more and more frequently and becomes an unyielding friend. I use this friend to filter out what I have forgotten, for what is forgotten is unnecessary to remember. The subconscious manipulates memory, just as the wind commands a kite on an invisible level. New, intricate webs of memory form an uneven sieve, leaving behind lumps that resemble cheese—sweet yet containing gritty, hard bits."}
{"trans": "His broad and upright thorax concealed the thunderous roars of his ancestors when they chased fierce beasts. The pelvis violently indented, with sharp, prominent bones indicating the presence of powerful muscle groups once attached there, like the ropes of Yellow River纤夫, pulling the entire body along with a wall lizard's clinging motion. There were also his limbs, like the long and beautiful tusks of an African elephant, emitting a smooth, glossy sheen."}
{"trans": "I had to wait several years before I could dispel my lingering resentment and acknowledge that day was a perilous turning point in my life. It was not the art teacher's mockery that made me abandon the painting of the withered rose, but rather the dazzling brilliance of your talent, which made me, with a gesture of regret, break my brush by myself. What is regret like? Like a small mole on one's body—only the person themselves knows its location and the process of its emergence."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, losing strands like falling leaves, which fell in clusters, brushing against my arms as if in the drizzle of night. In the distance and near, many cars honked desperately; the sky, gradually darkening, spread out like a vast expanse of misty and colorful lake. In the lowest window of a house across the street, a faint white curl of cooking smoke rose hesitantly, as if unsure where the sky lay."}
{"trans": "She was carrying two water pitchers in her hands, which reminded me of a woman walking with spirit on a thin rope. It was all due to her waist; her waist was so soft, soft enough to make me feel as if I were eating Suzhou's cowhide candy. Not only her waist, my diary says well: she had a set of curves as beautiful as clouds and mist, as enchanting as the moon reflected on water, weaving a great net of enchantment!"}
{"trans": "\"Because of your language, you remain silent, sinking to the deepest depths, letting yourself disappear.\" Losing language, thus losing oneself, losing the substance of existence, Yang Lian thus realizes that he has become a \"ghost\"; ghosts drift between cities, watching coldly (like insects, ghosts are also \"it,\" capable only of watching), watching the complete annihilation of \"meaning.\" There is the sea, yet the port holds no meaning for you."}
{"trans": "A lamp is far apart from another lamp; between segments of brightness lies segments of darkness. My shadow appears in the light at times and disappears into the darkness at others. The wind comes out of nowhere, wave after wave, stirring the colorful leaves, as if stirring the impressions of life. I feel as if I am this empty, coming wind; only when I shed and whirl up the colorful leaves can I catch a glimpse of my own existence."}
{"trans": "But we stood on the open land — my father, my brother, our relatives, and many villagers who had sweated and toiled under the scorching sun and the rain and wind — listening in silence to the distant thunder, motionless, with no one wanting to seek shelter from the coming northwest rain. Our hearts were heavier than the sky in drought, and we all remained silent, for our hearts were also skies awaiting rain, and this rain of the heart seemed even more tragic and relentless than the northwest rain, falling endlessly into the heavens."}
{"trans": "Imagine, if Tang Bohu and Qianlong were both considered \"first-rate poets of ancient China,\" then we would have to quietly burn the entire anthology of \"Complete Tang Poetry\" to the ground. The same applies to calligraphy: an astonishingly high price paid for a mediocre brushwork is like a heap of gold that tips the scales of Chinese calligraphy history. In the face of such a situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the cultural lineage fades, a small hill becomes a peak; when strong wings have flown away, broken feathers fill the sky of a鹏.\""}
{"trans": "It happens suddenly, as if the girl has received a divine command from heaven, convulsing abruptly without any warning. The soft girl curls up like a hard rolling pin, every muscle gleaming like iron. Her tiny body arches like a bow ready to shoot an arrow, rebounding violently on the pale, snow-white hospital bed. Countless beads of sweat drip from this strange human rainbow, pattering down like melting snow from the eaves in spring."}
{"trans": "This released power, lonely yet powerful, follows patterns yet breaks them, intoxicated and poetic, resembling the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu treated the brush pen as a stumbling, drunken step, swaying unsteadily, dancing with his hands and feet, his posture graceful and his energy full. He completed all his movements in a continuous flow, then threw down his cup and laughed heartily, falling soundly asleep. Zhang Xu did not know that his drunken steps were precisely the steps of Tang Dynasty culture."}
{"trans": "But just as I was holding my breath, fully absorbed in listening, suddenly and simultaneously, everyone fell silent. Again, that cicada startled me! It was as if the cicada's song had tied my heart tightly with a rope, and then suddenly, without warning, the rope was loosened. My heart, unprepared, scattered like a wave striving to leap into the sky, only to accidentally fall onto the beach! When did summer cross the threshold and come near me? I didn't even know!"}
{"trans": "I once wept bitterly for your humiliation and despair. My tears flowed like a stream, clear as crystal, yet they could not wash away your thick filth, only clearing the veil from my eyes. These tears could not moisten your hearts of iron and stone, but only quenched the anxious and fervent flame in my heart. Now, I laugh at your suffering, a laugh like thunder roaring, not coming after the storm, but echoing before the storm."}
{"trans": "I gradually came to understand that in the face of disaster, one cannot use the grammar of disaster; there is another kind of grammar that directly leads to a poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From that moment on, my life state changed completely. Every time I read chapters such as \"Autumn Waters,\" \"Free Soaring,\" \"The Unity of Things,\" and \"The World\" from Zhuangzi, it was as if I were looking at electrocardiograms related to myself. For such an overly familiar sage, I found it difficult to offer a calm and objective commentary, so I could only retreat and avoid."}
{"trans": "You pressed your forehead against the brocade embroidery. When the sun was on this side, it made the gold threads scorching hot, but now they have cooled down. The people of the past struggled through their lives, their deeds gradually covered in dust; when descendants hung out their clothes, they shook down the dust, which danced in the yellow sunlight. If memories had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor, sweet and secure, like clearly remembered joy, sweet and melancholic, like forgotten sorrow."}
{"trans": "It is precisely this depth that brings them close to life, allowing us, thousands of years later, to still feel close to them. The bustling life of Yang Yuhui, I imagine, is like a ceramic soup pot, smooth and cool as jade, sitting by the feet, its water gradually cooling down, evoking a gentle sense of resistance. Su Qing, however, is more like a small red clay stove, with its own independent fire, visible red flames, and audible crackling sounds, but it is more difficult to tend, requiring constant adding of coal and wood, with smoke that is suffocating."}
{"trans": "Like surging waves and terrifying tides, they strike against the emotions that have settled deep in your heart. In an instant, you feel that the cicadas' cries seem to snatch away your lingering sorrows, as if they were being dragged away by wild waves of sand. The urgency of the cicadas' song suddenly stops abruptly at its highest note, like a splendid piece of writing being violently torn apart. The resounding words scatter across the ground, falling with the sound of precious stones. Then, in silence, they become fragmented remnants of a once-glorious text, leaving only a sense of melancholy and sorrow. Is it not the song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here there is active youth, hot red hearts, no listless old men, only strong old boys. The silver-white moon wavers aimlessly in the hollow sky, as if weeping, hating her loneliness. ... There is also that swimming pool, always like a kind old grandmother, smiling with wrinkles all over her face. When she sees many lively children jump into the water like little mermaids, she bursts into great silver splashes of joy."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, it has been a lost wilderness. On one side of the wilderness are mysterious great craftsmen, unknown to us. On the other side is a modern woman, panic-stricken and confused. The kilns on both sides burn fiercely, like two beacons separated by thousands of mountains and rivers. Yet the signals they send are precise and accurate. Many other beacons are related to war, but these two are not. Across the bloody wars of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, only two clean wisps of smoke rise, echoing each other from afar."}
{"trans": "Lin Daiyu's brokenness lies in her all-consuming love; Sanmao's brokenness comes from a moment of clarity and transcendence after enduring countless hardships; Van Gogh's brokenness is the sun's golden knife cutting through him, causing continuous agony in the light; Beethoven's brokenness is the tragic symphony of life struck by the ultimate spiritual keys. If the brokenness of ordinary people reveals the purest and most beautiful light of humanity, then the brokenness of these outstanding souls is like silver lotus flowers blooming across the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "How many times a day should you wash your face? Even if you wash it several times, it still won't be clean. As for the eyes, if you don't wash them, they will always remain bright. The empty spaces can't serve the function of a mop or a broom, so there's no need to spend money on them. After all, people are naturally active and are born with the ability to avoid dust. Surprisingly, the air doesn't become thinner because the space is small. To observe human breathing, we use cigarettes as visible air. We take one puff in and exhale three, letting the smoke spiral up to the ceiling, like a cloud covering the sky. After observing the abundance of things on the ground, we can then look up and contemplate the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "Knowing oneself but not knowing others, merely gathering in a corner, dying old without ever meeting others—this is the way of the summer insect that cannot comprehend ice, the frog in the well, and the donkey in the mill. Only when one knows others can one truly know oneself; just as the Queen of Hearts' fan, it must be able to expand before it can be retracted. The more one knows, the broader one's horizons become; one must scatter oneself throughout the world, seep into all things, observing their size and shape, their weight and density, only then can one gradually and gradually discern one's true self, analyzing even the finest details."}
{"trans": "The songs flow like drifting clouds and flowing water, relieving one's worries and allowing one to wander leisurely within. They are also like surging waves and terrifying tides, striking against the emotions settled in your heart, and in an instant, you feel that the cicadas' calls seem to snatch away your tightly held worries like wild waves washing away sand. The urgency of the cicadas' song suddenly stops at the peak of its notes, more like a splendid essay being violently torn apart. The resounding words scatter on the ground, falling with the sound of precious stones, and then become a fragmentary and incomplete piece, leaving only a sense of melancholy and sorrow."}
{"trans": "What is there that is not empty? The affairs of God are unknown to man; the affairs of man, however, are constructed and continued in meaning even amidst the encirclement of fate—perhaps one might say, in a helpless manner—thus saving the present and also the eternal. Therefore, \"eternal recurrence\" is by no means a \"complete affirmation of earthly life,\" but merely states that man cannot escape earthly life, not even death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence toward the eternal, that is, man's looking upward to the heavens—the great music has always filled the sky and the earth."}
{"trans": "Looking at Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings, the experience is entirely different. That feeling is like reading the pastoral poems of Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei in the deep of night; with just a few strokes and a faint ink, it does not stir up intense emotions in our hearts, but instead calms them down. It is not something that fills our hearts with something new, but rather it washes away the worldly worries that were already crowding our hearts. It is like a mountain stream after a heavy rain; at first, the water is muddy, but when the rain clears and the sky turns blue, the stream becomes clear, and the mud and filth in the mountain are all washed away."}
{"trans": "This sound was at times slow and hurried, high and low, loud and deep, broken and continuous. Sometimes it resembled the harmonious resonance of golden bells and jade chimes, sometimes the solemn tones of the great bell Huangzhong and the grand bell Dalü, sometimes like big and small pearls falling on a jade plate, sometimes like red coral and white coral sinking into the sea, sometimes like plucking a simple zither, sometimes like dancing with lightning, sometimes like a hundred birds singing in chorus, sometimes like a rabbit falling and a hawk rising. My imagination soared, I could not control myself, my heart bloomed with joy, and a breeze of inspiration surged from my pen. The dead words seemed to come alive again, and I felt as if my youth had returned. I rarely experienced such a state of mind in my lifetime, and it is something even harder to share with outsiders."}
{"trans": "Perhaps clouds are meant to drift in the sky, unlike the sun with its fiery chariot, so they never descend to accept my warm hospitality. It must be just my illusion, though this illusion is undeniably beautiful. If the blue sky is an undecipherable book, then clouds must be its silent annotations. My speeding car tracks translate the language of clouds onto the road surface, becoming the latest commentary. The sky narrates with changing shades of blue, clouds sketch with pure hands, and then it's up to my eyes to print it. We are all telling the story of a夸父 (Kua Fu), the mythological figure who chased the sun."}
{"trans": "I couldn't eat it on the plane, but when I returned to the United States, I tried it again and found it too oily and too spicy, which was nothing like the occasional sausage rolls my father used to make. Next door to our home in Shanghai was the Cheesecake Café, which had just moved from wartime Tianjin. Every morning they baked bread, sending out a scent alarm, a powerful, fragrant gust that swept through the air like a long, sweeping wind. It was the softest kind of alarm, yet it was not at the right time, waking people up unnecessarily, like an annoying spring scene that one can't help but feel helpless about. Having this neighbor \"Fang\" was indeed a kind of disturbance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like the sugar-coated medicine given to children, or the electric rabbit that lures dogs in a dog race. A few minutes or even a few days of happiness make us live a lifetime, enduring much suffering. We hope for happiness, wish it to stay, and long for it to return again — these three sentences summarize the entire history of human effort. While we pursue and wait, life quietly slips away. Perhaps we are merely chips in the game of time, living our entire lives as sacrifices for the years, never thinking of happiness at all."}
{"trans": "There is a dark silk fabric of a kind called \"Xilanglv,\" covered with large black shadows, brimming with wind and thunder. There is also a Japanese silk fabric of a light lake-blue color, shimmering with the patterns of wood and water; at regular intervals, two blossoms of tea-cup size float on the water, carved with iron-like strokes and silver-like lines, resembling the stained glass windows of medieval chapels, with red glass edged with heavy iron. The most common fabric found on the market is of various unnamed colors—neither blue, nor gray, nor yellow—only suitable for background use. These are called neutral colors, also known as protective colors, civilized colors, and mixed colors."}
{"trans": "It comes from her movements; every step she takes, every stretch of her back, every flick of her hair, every glance, every bow, even the slightest movement of her sleeves and the gentle sway of her skirt—all flow like honey, like the gentle ripple of wind. How could we not rejoice and admire her? Most adorable is her soft waist; ancient people spoke of willows swaying in the wind, and in \"Dream of the Red Chamber,\" they described Qingwen's \"serpent waist,\" both referring to the delicately soft curve of the waist. But the waist I love is so soft it is like Suzhou's cowhide candy, making my tongue full of sweetness and my teeth full of softness. With such a soft waist, her hands and feet naturally exude an air of elegance and grace."}
{"trans": "Beside, some bottles of wine are leaning crookedly, and there's already not much wine left. Alas, I don't drink wine. Otherwise, at such a moment, sipping a little would surely be a delightful pleasure. \"Raising a cup to invite the bright moon,\" the moon would shyly slip into your cup. A gentle breeze passes by, and you can hear the pines on both mountain sides rustling softly. As the branches sway, the lights become more and more flickering, like mischievous children playing hide and seek with you. They harmonize with the shimmering scales jumping on the river surface, as if playing a symphony together. What a dreamy scene of earthly life this is!"}
{"trans": "I can no longer explain clearly. On the stage, with a real sun shining upon it, there is such a melancholy. Between art and reality, there is a place where they overlap, making everything seem hazy. It's like holding a matchstick burning in the sunlight, slowly drifting, so that the faint orange-yellow flame is not clearly visible, yet I can more distinctly sense my own hand as a temporary thing in the sunlight... The maid on stage sang for a while, holding a tea tray, and with a graceful posture of parting flowers and swaying willows, she moved from room to room, crossed countless thresholds, and arrived at the study, bowing deeply to the young master, then raising the tea tray high to her brow."}
{"trans": "I saw a calico cat lying lazily against a broken, neglected wall, where the morning glory flowers bloomed in a vivid mix of deep green and purple. Indifferently, the cat stretched its lazy limbs. In the hazy night, I saw street lamps casting the shadow of a transformer box on the sidewalk haphazardly onto a white wall of a construction site, intertwining with the swaying shadows of the roadside trees, creating a scene that looked like Romeo singing a love song from the balcony where Juliet stood. I saw the face of the poet Zhou Mengdie, exactly fitting into a small window of a moving bus as I waved him goodbye, as if the entire bus, with its grandeur, was serving as a frame for his portrait."}
{"trans": "You imagine that innocent heart, pure and loving everything, which is now clearly visible in the faint morning mist; no matter how you call out to it, it never returns to your bosom. How deeply lacking this is! Thus, Pingbo feels suffocated and, like the gentle spring breeze whispering among the green trees, he earnestly and softly confides in you the intangible memories of his childhood. Though he cannot dwell permanently in those childhood days, if he could invite more companions to wander through them, it would somewhat alleviate his sense of emptiness. The melancholy would then not linger endlessly on his tongue."}
{"trans": "You could also say it marks the beginning of the Chinese people's journey toward modernity, but which nation's steps toward modernity were as hurried, anxious, self-doubting, and chaotic as those in Shanghai? You could also say it is a city civilization rising in opposition to agrarian civilization, but which city civilization was so constantly coveted, disintegrated, surrounded, and overshadowed by the vast power of rural forces, as Shanghai was? In short, it is a great paradox: when you look at its filth, it shines with dazzling brilliance; when you worship its might, it turns around and lets you see its scarred back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the reality was quite the opposite. I sat quietly there, listening to the sound of raindrops falling above my head. At that moment, the sound was more powerful than silence, and I felt boundless joy within me, as if I had drunk celestial dew and inhaled the essence of enlightenment, leaving me feeling as if I were about to soar into the heavens. The sound varied in speed, sometimes slow and sometimes quick, sometimes high and sometimes low, sometimes loud and sometimes soft, sometimes continuous and sometimes broken. At times it resembled the resonant tones of gongs and bells, at times the solemn notes of the great bell, at times the gentle clinking of large and small pearls on a jade plate, at times the deep and mysterious sound of red coral and white coral sinking into the sea, at times the delicate melody of a simple zither, at times the sudden crack of lightning, at times the cacophony of a hundred birds singing in unison, at times the sudden fall of a rabbit startled by a hawk. My mind swirled with endless imagination, unable to control myself, my heart bloomed with joy, and my pen danced with inspiration."}
{"trans": "Numerous advertisements and shops around him buzzed with noise, and car horns blared. He was like the legendary figure from ancient tales who dreamed of a lifetime in one night, but he had only slept for a single night and woke up, without having had such a dream—rather, there was a sense of compassion. ... The Taoist priest knelt down in front of a hardware store, but of course, the people there had no money to give him. He seemed to look down on them, and with a sense of aimlessness, he simply knelt and bowed once. Then he got up, knocking with a \"tuo-tuo\" sound, transitioning to the door of the neighboring tobacco and paper shop, and then again \"kneeling in the dust,\" his head slumped sideways, his movements like a black stream of淤blood, slowly blooming like a black chrysanthemum."}
{"trans": "Why not? In spring, birds sing; in autumn, crickets chirp; in summer, mosquitoes make a thunderous sound. At night, insects awaken while birds sleep. Storms do not come every day, and dogs do not bark without a reason. Hens do not crow unless they lay eggs. Only humans make sounds through speech, actions, and machines, creating noise anytime and anywhere. Even when alone in a room with no one to respond to, they can turn on a gramophone, listen to the radio, or even emit thunder-like snoring while sleeping. Of course, language is not merely sound, but when it is unpleasant, unwanted, or heard through walls and distance, words lose their sharpness and form, becoming a fluctuating, noisy mass, as meaningless as the crowing of a rooster or the barking of a dog."}
{"trans": "As time passes, the past remains forever behind, unable to be recalled back to the time when we first met beneath the blooming peach blossoms. Yet in human memory, the lingering charm or lingering wounds of the past often resurface, surging like waves against the shore, making the present an extension of those past echoes, carrying them further and deeper. If life were a pre-bound, numbered blank book, the disturbances of past experiences to a person would be like writing too heavily on one page, causing ink stains to seep into the following pages, impossible to erase. Naturally, one need not destroy the old pages for satisfaction, just as there is no need to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower after the Yellow Crane has already flown away. Yet, it is necessary to open up the old records by lamplight, to proceed where one should, and to stop where one should."}
{"trans": "The vast northwest consists of barren basalt mountains and vast deserts where solitary plumes of smoke rise straight into the sky. You, a geology student, carry a large leather geology satchel on your shoulder, made of canvas, and you have been traveling for twenty years. Twenty years of tents, drifting like a small boat among the dunes of sand, illuminated by a crescent moon. Can the bell of Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou City ring out at midnight to reach the traveler's boat? Your wife, that beautiful and elegant lady, is watching you, her longing net spread across her face, searching for the heart of love that has long since departed. You return home once a year, planting a cluster of bamboo each time at the gate, but you leave again, leaving behind clusters of bamboo leaves shaped like the character \"个.\""}
{"trans": "If life is a pre-bound, numbered blank book, then past events disturbing a person are like when writing on a particular page with too much pressure, causing the ink to seep into the following pages, leaving indelible marks. Of course, one need not destroy the old pages for satisfaction, just as there is no need to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower after the Yellow Crane has already flown away. Yet, it is necessary to open up old records by the light, to proceed where one should and stop where one must. After embracing life as a whole, one can be generous and tolerant toward past events or new things, giving them their proper place and meaning. If it is a beautiful thing, one can see from the bud of this matter what kind of branches grow out of it; if it is a sorrowful thing, one can also see a tender branch emerging from the gloomy weather and stretching toward the bright sky."}
{"trans": "Everything seemed distant from me, even my own shadow in the bright moonlight appeared hazy, more misty than smoke. Just as I was about to turn around and go to sleep, I hesitated for a step, and the fleeting remnants of my dream suddenly paused, though it quickly resumed flying away like an arrow with its tip detached."}
{"trans": "The last hope is merely an aesthetic support. Just like a sunken ship in icy sea, utterly hopeless, yet looking up at the scene of stormy clouds rushing by; just like there's no way to survive under the wild slashes, yet looking down at the blood-splattered patterns. Aesthetic support is the last support."}
{"trans": "What we have gathered in the past and will gather in the future are merely seeds. When you are a wish wandering in the mist, so am I, wandering among the same mist. We seek each other out; from our yearnings, dreams grow, endless and boundless."}
{"trans": "In this purity, the dish is oneself, the cook is oneself, and the eater is still oneself. Just as love is oneself, knowing who loves is oneself, and remembering the love is still oneself. One sips oneself bit by bit through the cup of time, and in the end, one gets drunk on oneself."}
{"trans": "The long pants cling tightly, making it impossible to lift the feet. The mind is pure as a sheet of paper, blank as a newborn infant, bidding farewell to the sea, bidding farewell to a lonely seagull circling in the sky. I will return, to speak of the dust of the eight directions and nine realms. Pick up the umbrella and the shoes, pick up all the myriad things of the human world."}
{"trans": "Unpredictable. I only hope that, even as a human flaw, it would present itself properly. Like the furrowed brow of a noble warrior, rather than the chaotic struggle of a group of ragged soldiers at night; like the thousand-year standoff of two snow peaks, rather than a tangle of vines wrapping around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was exceptionally beautiful. The sky seemed like a blue ritual object fired during the Jingde period of the Ming Dynasty, deep and boundless. Through the huge silver table-like moon, one could still see the metallic blue glow behind it. The moonlight couldn't withstand the dyeing of the blue sky, and it drifted faintly like diluted ink, thread by thread."}
{"trans": "Repeating watching the same movie is like spitting out the food you've already eaten and chewing it again. At that moment, our heads turned golden, as if covered with wheat awns. I remember that a character in Gorky's book once said that young lovers should not meet again, for it's like a skeleton rising from the ground..."}
{"trans": "As soon as I close my eyes, I think of it; as soon as I open them, I crave it. But when all of this suddenly rushes upon me, almost drowning me, I can't help but wonder what exactly I want anymore. My heart aches painfully, as if tightly bound by threads of silk, as if scorched by drops of candle wax, as if tossing and turning on a vast, endless sea."}
{"trans": "The faintest echo of your sighs will become its voice. After life is veiled, it is just like your greatest soul, hidden and concealed. When life speaks, all the winds become words; when life speaks again, your smile on the lips and tears in the eyes will also become words."}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality gradually faded. With the passage of seasons, plum blossoms withered and cranes aged; culture became a purposeless waste. The closed moral perfection led to an overall immorality. The advancement of civilization was thus canceled, leaving only a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks, tucked between the pages of the nation's spiritual history."}
{"trans": "Granting religious spirit a pass based on science and philosophy is like using intellect and reasoning to fall in love, inevitably suppressing the passion of life and exhausting the charm of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is like treating family background and property as the criteria for marriage, turning children into breeding machines and making them spiritually castrated."}
{"trans": "In fact, all destruction is concrete, and all委屈 are hard to express, so those answers are also questionable. There's no need to doubt the results—withered grass and broken rubble carry the suffering of countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I willingly face all of this in a perilous situation with no protective mechanisms, just as I would remove my gloves to touch an old man's wounds."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I look at myself like a child copying a passage from a long hymn; when God created the first man, the angels sang that hymn. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom; that book was written on the first page of emotion before time began."}
{"trans": "Even the great events spanning thousands of years, or the grand endeavors connecting myriad lands, if they belong to culture, are always shouldered by a pair of old, weary shoulders. Like smugglers, like fugitives, they evade and secretly inquire their way, searching for a place to entrust their legacy. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, thus inevitably destined to remain unexplained during one's lifetime."}
{"trans": "There is no need to doubt the outcome; withered grass and ruined rubble carry the scars of disasters from ancient times to the present. I willingly face all of this in perilous situations without any protective measures, just as I would remove my gloves to touch an old man's wounds. This act of touching often provokes deep contemplation: as the foundation of our lives, Chinese civilization is also full of wounds. Yet how has it managed to avoid total collapse?"}
{"trans": "Who could possibly attach the meaning that has already been created and send it to you along with your birth certificate? After all, birth itself is a request for meaning directed at the one being born, asking you to seek or create meaning. It's like a publishing contract in which you are paid in advance, with the term lasting a lifetime. Of course, you are not the creditor but the debtor; it is life that is demanding meaning from you, and you have no right to complain."}
{"trans": "Those uneven inks, those red-stamped titles, those crossed-out names, those rows of exclamation marks, those restrained appeals, those repeated corrections—combined into a terrifying sound, overwhelming us all at once. It's as if just a few strands of white hair on the corner of a room, or a half piece of torn fabric among the leaves at the tree's tip, could instantly transport us back to that era we dare not think about anymore."}
{"trans": "Some fall on the hairpin of the vegetable picker, some stick to the black coat of the swallow, and others slide into the little stream to play. The river, like a thousand wandering flute players, accompanies the schoolchildren on their way home singing songs. When mischievous children carry their books on top of their straw hats and wade across the river with two shoes in hand, will spore infants pop out from the flute holes, bite the child's sleeve, and finally return to the mother's soil of wild ferns?"}
{"trans": "Soul, return! Return to your old dwelling. When he spoke in Hokkien and made people laugh heartily, when he spoke in Beijing dialect and left people staring blankly, why didn't he ever defend himself: here, his Chu accent is as deep as the land and mountains, as vast as the heavens and spirits? Every tone of the officiant is like the tone of his father reciting the \"Memorial to the Imperial Court,\" melodious and sorrowful, each tone striking you down."}
{"trans": "He was too thin, his sunken skin unable to fill the gaps between his ribs, making the ribs look like a steel bridge spanning across. His heartbeat was fierce and heavy, like a bleeding sun, burning hollowly, emitting the sounds of flames and caverns. Mei Ying had once heard Yu Bei Zhi's heartbeat—deep and resonant, pulsing steadily and rhythmically through his well-developed muscles, like coal buried deep within the earth's crust."}
{"trans": "From inn to inn, without settling in mountain villages or riverside spots, what is there that I can pray for? Perhaps youth? But how fleeting it is. I am like a man who has found a treasure, carrying pearls and gold with a careless net, only to realize that the longer I walk, the lighter I become, and youth has already scattered into dust. Perhaps it is scriptures and classics? But can a wealth of knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "On the mountain ridges of his hometown, when greeting someone from afar, one doesn't use the soft \"Ah—\" of city dwellers, nor the exaggerated \"Wa—\" of southerners. \"Ah\" and \"Wa\" don't travel far before being swallowed by the mountains. Only the deep, heavy, long, and desolate \"Er ha—\" can soar like an eagle for a long time. Now, like mist falling from the sky, the eagles have vanished, and endless feelings of home fill Shen Zhanping's heart with intense warmth and passion."}
{"trans": "Hurry up and escape from the political mire you have completely failed to understand, and chase after the long-lost poetic sentiment. Chasing poetic sentiment is also chasing oneself—the self once familiar to the Nine Provinces, the self clung to by one's wife, the self that thought it had found but actually lost. This time, turning back to chase, you are accompanied by the morning glow, witnessed by the flowing river, encouraged by the cries of apes, and guided by myriad mountains. Thus, the lifeboat, which has become increasingly heavy with burdens, once again transforms into a light boat."}
{"trans": "Although airplanes can be imagined as Zhuangzi's carefree journey or Liezi's wind riding, they are not very appealing to watch. How different they are from the long train rides, with their hypnotic rhythm, ever-changing scenery, and the view from the window, which seems to be both within the world and beyond it. Therefore, when traveling abroad, wherever the double-track railway can reach, I always stand on the platform — a real \"Long Pavilion\" — waiting for that majestic train to roar and rush into the station, carrying me to distant lands."}
{"trans": "Opposed to prominence is the ordinary, opposed to the officialdom is the common people. More effective in concealment than the dense vegetation in mountain forests is the ordinary life of common people in a small town. The concealment in mountain forests still preserves and boasts a sense of aloofness, but such aloofness is ultimately insincere. The concealment in the streets of a small town not only does not require deliberately torturing or destroying life, but can instead make life very comfortable, allowing existence to rest in a quiet and convenient corner. It can almost dissolve one's being from the outside in, thus becoming the highest form of concealment. To speak of concealment may be too narrow; after all, in my mind, the image of a small bridge, flowing water, and nearby houses, as well as the longing for tender lotus and game fish, all represent ecological imagery of a religious life philosophy."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze is not acquainted with me, why does it enter my silk curtain?"}
{"trans": "From then on, I have no heart for fine nights; let the bright moon set behind the western pavilion."}
{"trans": "The candle has a heart, still shedding tears for parting, weeping until dawn for others."}
{"trans": "Chang'e should regret stealing the elixir, with endless longing in the vast sea and clear sky night after night."}
{"trans": "Three visits to persuade the wise man, with constant deliberation on the world's affairs; in two dynasties, the old minister's loyal heart was devoted to the country."}
{"trans": "Three divisions and strategies in the struggle, a feather rising through the clouds for a thousand ages."}
{"trans": "A tune of \"Hou Ting Hua,\" full of sorrow, unbearable to listen to."}
{"trans": "In olden days, the swallows that once flew in the halls of Wang and Xie now fly into the homes of ordinary people."}
{"trans": "Regretful, I have no way to meet Fan Li; the misty trees stretch eastward by the Five Lakes."}
{"trans": "East wind did not favor Zhou Lang, and the spring in the Bronze雀 locked the two Qiaos."}
{"trans": "Victory or defeat is not something soldiers can predict, but to bear shame and endure humiliation is the way of a true man."}
{"trans": "How could one rule as emperor for four decades, yet not match the peace of the Lu family's worry-free life?"}
{"trans": "The jade scepter leaves the phoenix palace, iron cavalry surrounds the dragon city."}
{"trans": "Why should the Qiang flute lament over willows, When spring breeze never reaches the Jade Gate Pass."}
{"trans": "The golden sands have worn through iron armor in a hundred battles; I'll never return until I break Loulan."}
{"trans": "When Qin shi mingyue, Han shi guan, ten thousand miles of long march, people have not returned."}
{"trans": "Soldiers on guard look at the border's changing colors, longing to return with sorrowful faces."}
{"trans": "Shoot the horse first to kill the rider; capture the bandit leader first to subdue the rebels."}
{"trans": "The sea of sand stretches with ice a hundred zhang thick, and gloomy clouds gather in sorrow across ten thousand miles."}
{"trans": "The forest is dark, the grass startles the wind; the general shoots at night with his bow."}
{"trans": "The great desert's sand is like snow, and the Yan Mountains' moon is like a hook."}
{"trans": "The farmer works in the midday sun, his sweat drips into the soil beneath the crops."}
{"trans": "A single rider on red dust, the queen laughs, no one knows it's lychees coming."}
{"trans": "A thousand gold fur coats, a horse with five kinds of flowers, call your son to bring them out and exchange for fine wine, to share with you and eliminate the sorrow of ages."}
{"trans": "To cross the Yellow River, ice blocks the channel; to climb Mount Taihang, snow fills the mountains."}
{"trans": "The Son of Heaven calls, but I won't get on the boat; I proudly declare myself the immortal wine lover."}
{"trans": "The divine beauty concentrates in the marvels of nature, and the yin and yang divide the light from the dark."}
{"trans": "I have a wandering soul that cannot be called back, the rooster's cry turns the world bright with dawn."}
{"trans": "Looking at the vast universe, I weep in sorrowful solitude."}
{"trans": "Endless falling leaves rustle down, endless rushing rivers flow on."}
{"trans": "The spring wind is favorable, my horse's hooves are swift; in one day I see all the flowers of Chang'an."}
{"trans": "Zhuangzi dreamed of a butterfly in the morning, and the King of the Spring Heart entrusted his sorrow to the cuckoo."}
{"trans": "Solitary smoke rises straight in the vast desert, the long river reflects the round setting sun."}
{"trans": "Alone in the secluded bamboo grove, I play the zither and let out a long, resonant cry."}
{"trans": "The water plummets three thousand feet straight down, seeming as if the Milky Way has fallen from the ninth heaven."}
{"trans": "Windows frame the western hills' eternal snow, and the eastern Wu's thousand-mile ships dock at the gate."}
{"trans": "Wild flowers gradually enchant the eyes, and the short grass can just cover the horse's hooves."}
{"trans": "In the Southern Dynasties, four hundred and eighty temples, how many pagodas and towers are shrouded in mist and rain."}
{"trans": "Rain falls heavily on the Qingming Festival, travelers on the road wish to break their souls."}
{"trans": "Without knowing who cut the fine leaves, the February spring wind is like a pair of scissors."}
{"trans": "April's flowers have all faded in the world, but peach blossoms in the mountain temple just begin to bloom."}
{"trans": "In the world of the sea, true friends are always near, even if separated by the horizon."}
{"trans": "May those in Luoyang ask about me if they have the chance; my pure heart is like ice in a jade vessel."}
{"trans": "Grieve a cup more, my friend, for beyond Yangguan, there will be no old friends."}
{"trans": "I send my sorrowful heart to the bright moon, accompanying you all the way to the west of Yelang."}
{"trans": "The depth of Peach Blossom Spring's waters reaches a thousand feet, yet it cannot match Wang Lun's affection for me."}
{"trans": "A single sail fades into the blue sky, Only the Yangtze River flows to the horizon."}
{"trans": "Cerulean bamboo forest temple, distant bell sounds at dusk."}
{"trans": "Closer to home, my feelings grow more timid; I dare not ask the passing strangers."}
{"trans": "This night, hearing the willow being cut in the song, who wouldn't feel longing for their homeland?"}
{"trans": "War flames span three months, a family letter is worth ten thousand gold."}
{"trans": "Who says the tiny grass heart can repay the spring sunshine's warmth."}
{"trans": "The flute sound seems to come from among the reeds, and white birds fly up in a line, startled suddenly."}
{"trans": "The tide-breaker stands proudly on the wave's crest, holding the red flag high, never letting it get wet."}
{"trans": "Innumerable, along the roads north, south, east, and west."}
{"trans": "Willow trees in green smoke, the morning chill is light; Red apricot branches, spring's delight is in bloom."}
{"trans": "Early stay half the journey through fragrant grass path, still cold, about to rain in the late spring day."}
{"trans": "The night is quiet, the wind is fine, and the fragrance lingers late; unaware that by dawn, the southern branches are blooming in full."}
{"trans": "Why need shallow green or deep red? Naturally, it is the finest among flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees had feelings, they would not be so green like this!"}
{"trans": "Moonlight cold, osmanthus leaves drift yellow."}
{"trans": "Long remembered is the parting scene, on the Jingshu楼, with the bright moonlight like water."}
{"trans": "When the night is still and the wind is calm, I long to return; only the river reflects the bright moon like a piece of jade."}
{"trans": "Dreams of the old country's mountains and rivers are broken, separated by layers of mist and water."}
{"trans": "The silk belt's heart-shaped knot is not yet tied, and the river's tide has already become calm."}
{"trans": "Going away, away, through miles of misty waves, the evening haze deepens, and the southern sky stretches wide."}
{"trans": "Wiping tears, I asked the flowers, but they remained silent; the fallen red petals fluttered past the swing."}
{"trans": "Fallen flowers, the person stands alone; light rain, swallows fly in pairs."}
{"trans": "A lonely tomb a thousand miles away, where can I speak of my sorrow?"}
{"trans": "Day by day I think of you, yet cannot see you; we share the same river Jiangling."}
{"trans": "Though the mountain vows remain, the silk letter cannot be entrusted."}
{"trans": "The old events of the Six Dynasties flow with the river, only cold mist and withered grass gather green."}
{"trans": "With a feather fan in hand and a silk scarf tied around his waist, he talked and laughed as the warships turned to ashes in the river."}
{"trans": "At night, I heard several cries of cranes, all proclaiming that the royal army was about to arrive."}
{"trans": "To be born as Sun Zhongmou is the ideal!"}
{"trans": "Thirty achievements, dust and soil; eight thousand miles of journey, clouds and moonlight."}
{"trans": "Under the temple of Fuli, a piece of divine crows and the sound of drums for the community sacrifice."}
{"trans": "Drunk, I return, sword in hand, leaning on the west wind; the river's waves still stir my spirit."}
{"trans": "The river flows like a whale rushing, the mountains stand like a tiger crouching, and the natural barriers are not man-made."}
{"trans": "Mist obscures the pavilion, moon confuses the river crossing."}
{"trans": "The羌 flute plays on sunny days, and lotus-pickers sing by lantern light at night; fishermen and lotus gatherers enjoy themselves happily."}
{"trans": "In the fragrance of rice blossoms, we talk of a bountiful year, listening to the chorus of frogs."}
{"trans": "A hundred years, brief and fleeting, witness rise and fall; still, we gaze together at the moon of that time."}
{"trans": "Helpless, the flowers fall away; the swallows return, as if we've met before."}
{"trans": "Under the mountain, the orchid sprouts are short and soak in the stream; the sandy path among the pines is clean and free of mud, with the evening rain and the cuckoo's call echoing."}
{"trans": "The phoenix tree is further accompanied by drizzling rain, and by dusk, the raindrops fall one after another."}
{"trans": "The swallows fly by, asking where spring is, yet only the pond remains green on its own."}
{"trans": "I wish to ride the wind and return, yet I fear the jade pavilions and crystal palaces, for their lofty heights may not withstand the cold."}
{"trans": "Clearly a dream of the Hu Xu world, turning back, the east wind fills my clothes with tears."}
{"trans": "The vast sky of Chu stretches for thousands of miles under a clear autumn, with the water flowing away to the horizon, merging with the sky, and the autumn seems endless."}
{"trans": "Red beans grow in the southern land, how many branches will sprout in spring?"}
{"trans": "The sun rises in the east and rains in the west; they say it's not clear, yet it is clear."}
{"trans": "At Xie Ting, parting place, the scenery always brings sorrow."}
{"trans": "His achievements surpassed the three states, his fame was established through the Eight Array Diagram."}
{"trans": "Flowers should be plucked when in bloom, for there will come a time when no flowers remain but only empty branches."}
{"trans": "The sunset is infinitely beautiful, but it's just near dusk."}
{"trans": "Alas, on the third night of the ninth month, the dewdrops resemble pearls, and the moon shines like a bow."}
{"trans": "After gathering flowers to make honey, for whom is the hardship and for whom is the sweetness?"}
{"trans": "Thousands of miles of yellow clouds obscure the sun, while the north wind blows geese and snowflakes fall in abundance."}
{"trans": "Before the mountain, the sudden rain rushes over the stream, thoroughly washing away the heat of the human world."}
{"trans": "Water is the horizontal glance of the eyes, mountains are the gathered peaks of the brows."}
{"trans": "Light rain has passed, the wind makes the forest dance, breaking through the misty canopy of clouds."}
{"trans": "Passersby outside the wall, a beautiful woman laughs within."}
{"trans": "I hate you just like the moon on the river pavilion, briefly full then waning."}
{"trans": "I will draw the decorated bow like a full moon, look toward the northwest, and shoot at the celestial wolf."}
{"trans": "The flowing water never stays, the flying light swiftly sets westward."}
{"trans": "Brain short-circuited"}
{"trans": "I repaired the purple knife with mud and filled the hole."}
{"trans": "Laughing mouse, don't be too funny"}
{"trans": "Wada Xi is going to be eating prison food?"}
{"trans": "Ge ge ge laughing nonstop"}
{"trans": "I majored in university specially"}
{"trans": "Oh my god! Eating the watermelon and ending up with someone from your own side? This is going to be on TV!"}
{"trans": "The taste is too strong, can you all roll to Zhihu?"}
